Empty Clip - Top-down shooter RPG
by Alan Witkowski

Home Page:
https://github.com/jazztickets/emptyclip

----- DOWNLOADING -----

Download and extract the latest emptyclip-*-src.tar.gz from https://github.com/jazztickets/emptyclip/releases

OR

Clone the repository:
git clone https://github.com/jazztickets/emptyclip.git --recurse-submodule

----- BUILDING ON LINUX -----

-- Dependencies required --
ninja
cmake 2.8.12+
sdl2
sdl2_image
sqlite3 3.32.0+
freetype2
openal
libvorbis
libogg
zlib

-- Installing dependencies on Debian --
sudo apt install ninja-build cmake build-essential libsdl2-dev libsdl2-image-dev libopenal-dev libvorbis-dev libfreetype6-dev libsqlite3-dev sqlite3

-- Installing dependencies on Arch Linux --
sudo pacman -S base-devel ninja cmake sdl2 sdl2_image openal libvorbis libogg freetype2 sqlite

-- Build executable --
./build.sh

-- Run the game without installing --
cd working && ./emptyclip

-- Installing --
cd build/release
sudo ninja install

-- Uninstall --
cd build/release
cat install_manifest.txt | xargs sudo rm

----- COMMAND-LINE ARGUMENTS -----

Parameters with <> denote required values
Parameters with [] denote optional values

Test a level
-level <map file>

Run game fullscreen
-fullscreen

Run game in a window
-window

Disable audio
-noaudio

Start the mapeditor
-editor [level]

----- HOW TO PLAY -----

Press ESDF to walk around
Press Left-click to shoot your gun
Hold Right-click to enter aim mode
Press Mouse Button 4 to attack with your melee weapon
Hold A to sprint
Press Spacebar to pick up items, open doors, or activate switches
Press R to reload your gun
Press W to switch weapons
Press V to toggle your flashlight
Press C to open your inventory or see character stats
Hold Tab to view the map
Press Middle Mouse Button to drop an item on the inventory screen
Hold Alt to show more information on the inventory screen
Press Escape to open the game menu or quit the game in test mode
Press F1 to open the game menu
Press F2 to show technical stats

Save data is in %APPDATA%/emptyclip for Windows and ~/.local/share/emptyclip for Linux.
